              ":question/id": "45d74b50-fd9d-5d18-835d-a7e140278a34",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4069",
              ":question/problem": "Given that $3^{2x+3}=5,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Taking $\\log_3$ of both sides of the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n   \t3^{2x+3} \t\t\t\t&= 5 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\\log_3 \\left(3^{2x+3}\\right)\t&= \\log_3 (5) \\\\[3pt]\n\t2x+3 \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_3 (5) . \\\\[3pt]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)}{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(3)} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)}{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(3)}-3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)}{2\\operatorname{log}\u2061(3)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx -0.768\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n**Note:** We used the change of base formula to rewrite the right-hand side, as many calculators can only compute base $10$ logarithms."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "9a7784d8-f6a4-5e45-b03e-d76a27372c48",
