              ":question/problem": "Given that $3\\cdot 6^{x} = 9,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
              ":question/worked-solution": "First, we isolate the exponential on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {6}^{x} & =9 \\\\ {6}^{x} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n   \t6^x \t\t\t\t\t&= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\\log_6 \\left(6^x\\right)\t&= \\log_6 (3) \\\\[3pt]\n\tx \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_6 (3)\\\\[3pt]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\log(3)}{\\log(6)}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx 0.613\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."
